#4812
Card and Dice Tables~
   This alcove is quieter than the main floor, though no less charged with
tension.  A row of green felt-covered dice tables lines the south wall, each
one attended by a croupier in black and white.  A slate board behind them is
chalked with results of the last dozen rolls.  The rules are simple: call HI
or LO, roll the two dice -- seven or higher is HI, six or lower is LO.  An
exact seven means the house wins.
~
